      "en": "# Part of Fortune: How to Calculate It and What It Says About Your Wealth & Happiness\n\nEveryone talks about Sun signs, Moon signs, and rising signs. But almost nobody talks about the Part of Fortune — and that's a mistake.\n\nThe Part of Fortune (Pars Fortunae) is one of the oldest points in astrology, dating back to the Greeks. It shows where you find prosperity, well-being, and flow. It's the point of \"easy money\" and natural happiness.\n\n## How to Calculate Your Part of Fortune\n\nThe formula depends on whether you were born during the day or night:\n\n**Day births (Sun above the horizon):**\nPart of Fortune = Ascendant + Moon - Sun\n\n**Night births (Sun below the horizon):**\nPart of Fortune = Ascendant + Sun - Moon\n\nDon't worry about doing the math yourself — generate your free birth chart and it will be calculated for you.\n\n## What Your Part of Fortune Means by House\n\n### 1st House: Fortune Through Self-Expression\n\nYou find happiness and prosperity by being authentically yourself. Your personal brand, your appearance, and your unique approach to life are your greatest assets. You succeed when you stop trying to be like everyone else.\n\n### 2nd House: Fortune Through Material Security\n\nThis is the classic \"money\" placement. You find prosperity through building tangible assets, managing resources well, and valuing what you have. Your self-worth and net worth are connected.\n\n### 3rd House: Fortune Through Communication\n\nYou make money and find joy through words — writing, speaking, teaching, networking. Your mind and your ability to connect ideas are your greatest assets. Siblings and local community may bring opportunities.\n\n### 4th House: Fortune Through Home & Family\n\nYour prosperity comes from your roots, your home, and your family. Real estate, interior design, or working from home could be lucrative. Emotional security is more important to you than status.\n\n### 5th House: Fortune Through Creativity & Romance\n\nYou find happiness and money through creative expression, romance, and play. Art, entertainment, children, and speculation can bring prosperity. Your joy is your wealth.\n\n### 6th House: Fortune Through Service & Health\n\nYou prosper by helping others. Healthcare, wellness, daily work, and service-oriented roles bring both money and satisfaction. Your well-being is directly tied to your routine.\n\n### 7th House: Fortune Through Partnerships\n\nYour success comes through other people — business partners, clients, spouses. You thrive in one-on-one relationships. Your ability to collaborate and negotiate is your greatest asset.\n\n### 8th House: Fortune Through Transformation & Other People's Resources\n\nThis is the placement of inherited wealth, investments, taxes, insurance, and other people's money. You find prosperity through deep transformation and shared resources. Psychology and healing may also be indicated.\n\n### 9th House: Fortune Through Higher Learning & Travel\n\nYou prosper through education, philosophy, travel, and publishing. Your worldview and your ability to see the big picture bring opportunities. Teaching and writing about big ideas can be lucrative.\n\n### 10th House: Fortune Through Career & Public Image\n\nThis is the \"success\" placement. You find prosperity through your career, reputation, and public standing. Ambition and achievement come naturally. You're meant to be seen in your field.\n\n### 11th House: Fortune Through Groups & Innovation\n\nYour wealth comes through networks, friends, groups, and technology. You're a natural connector. Innovation, humanitarian work, and community building bring both money and joy.\n\n### 12th House: Fortune Through Spirituality & Surrender\n\nYou find prosperity through inner work, spirituality, and letting go. This is a mystical placement — you may attract money through behind-the-scenes work, institutions, or spiritual practices. Your wealth is often hidden or unconventional.\n\n## How to Use Your Part of Fortune\n\n1. **Generate your chart** to find your Part of Fortune sign and house\n2. **Focus on that area** — it's where flow comes naturally\n3. **Don't force it** — the Part of Fortune shows where you're already lucky, not where you need to struggle\n4. **Combine with your Sun and Moon** — the Part of Fortune works best when aligned with your core identity\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\nThe Part of Fortune is your personal prosperity GPS. It shows where the universe is already supporting you. Stop swimming upstream — follow your Part of Fortune and let the current carry you.\n\nYour birth chart can show your exact Part of Fortune placement. Generate your free chart to find your wealth direction.\n\n[Generate Your Free Birth Chart →](/natal)\n\nFor a deep, personalized wealth reading — including your Part of Fortune, money patterns, and best career directions — unlock the AI Career Report.\n\n[Unlock Your Career Report · $19.99](https://hanhan55.gumroad.com/l/zxccdv)\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is the Part of Fortune the same as the Lot of Fortune?\n\nYes. They're different names for the same point. \"Part\" and \"Lot\" are translations of the same Arabic concept.\n\n### Does the Part of Fortune guarantee wealth?\n\nNo. It shows where prosperity comes most naturally — but you still have to act. Think of it as fertile soil; you still have to plant seeds.\n\n### Why haven't I heard of this before?\n\nThe Part of Fortune is an ancient technique that fell out of favor in modern astrology. It's experiencing a revival as more astrologers rediscover traditional techniques.\n\n### Can my Part of Fortune change?\n\nNo. It's fixed at birth. But your relationship to it can evolve as you grow and align with its energy.\n\n## Related Articles\n\n- [What Career Is Right For Me? Astrology Guide](/blog/what-career-is-right-for-me-astrology)\n- [BaZi Career Direction: Find Your Element's Best Industry](/blog/bazi-career-direction-day-master)\n- [Saturn Return (Ages 27-30): Career Decisions](/blog/saturn-return-career-advice-27-30)"
